---
import SiteLayout from '../../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import TableActions from '../../../../components/TableActions.astro';
import QueryExamples from '../../../../components/QueryExamples.astro';
import { databases, databaseById } from '../../../../data/db';
import type { Database } from '../../../../data/types';
export function getStaticPaths() { return databases.map((db) => ({ params: { id: db.id }, props: { db } })); }
const { db } = Astro.props as { db: Database };
const shipping = ['northwind','shipping','shipping-logs'].includes(db.id);
const table = db.tables.find((table) => table.name === (db.id === 'chinook' ? 'Track' : db.id === 'northwind' ? 'Orders' : db.id === 'shipping' ? 'requests' : 'baseline')) ?? db.tables[0];
const sourceTable = (id: string, name: string, filter: Record<string, string | number>) => { const href = new URL(`/tables/${encodeURIComponent(name)}/`,databaseById.get(id)!.canonicalUrl); href.searchParams.set('rows',JSON.stringify({filter})); href.hash='data'; return href.href; };
---
<SiteLayout db={db} title={`${shipping ? 'Shipping investigation' : 'Guided exploration'} — ${db.name} | DemoDB`} description={`A guided path from ${db.name} records to their relationships, meanings and reproducible examples.`} canonical="/learn/">
 <section class="page-intro shell"><p class="eyebrow">A guided question</p><h1>{shipping ? 'What happened to order 11045?' : db.id === 'chinook' ? 'From a track to its artist.' : `Ask a question of ${db.name}.`}</h1><p>{shipping ? 'Follow a Northwind identifier into its synthetic Shipping companion, then inspect the original log evidence. Each source keeps its own schema and provenance.' : 'Start with a real record, follow a declared relationship, then change a prepared query and inspect the result.'}</p></section>
 <section class="shell section guided-journey"><ol>
 {shipping ? <>
  <li><h2>Find the order</h2><p><a class="text-link" href={sourceTable('northwind','Orders',{OrderID:11045})}>Open Northwind Orders · 11045 →</a></p><p>Northwind is the sample business database. The companion uses its identifiers for training; synthetic controls may use identifiers absent from Northwind.</p></li>
  <li><h2>Inspect the shipping request and routing state</h2><p><a class="text-link" href={sourceTable('shipping','requests',{order_id:11045})}>Find the synthetic request →</a> · <a class="text-link" href={sourceTable('shipping','current_routes',{order_id:11045})}>Inspect current routes →</a></p><p>Read <code>attempts</code>, <code>routes</code> and <code>workspace_state</code> together. The business clock is scenario state. Publication, receipt and assignment acceptance each establish different facts; none alone proves delivery.</p></li>
  <li><h2>Read the baseline before any replay</h2><p><a class="text-link" href={sourceTable('shipping-logs','baseline',{order_id:11045})}>Read original baseline observations →</a> · <a class="text-link" href={sourceTable('shipping-logs','carrierGateway',{order_id:11038})}>Compare the healthy 11038 carrier-gateway control →</a></p><p>The fixture baseline contains healthy 11038 and blocked requests 11045 and 11062. Sequence, clock domain, precision and immutable artifact byte ranges matter when correlating evidence. A missing booking is not proof that an external service was contacted.</p></li>
  <li><h2>Keep future examples separate</h2><p><a class="text-link" href={sourceTable('shipping-logs','recovery11045example',{order_id:11045})}>Inspect the labelled 11045 replay example →</a></p><p>Recovery example streams are separate synthetic future scenarios. They do not change baseline observations or establish that a live recovery occurred. The provider describes the 11062 replay as pending; its example records remain teaching inputs.</p></li>
  <li><h2>Compare the concepts and preserve the evidence</h2><p><a class="text-link" href="https://demodb.dev/concepts/?q=shipping">Compare shipping meanings across sources →</a> · <a class="text-link" href="/downloads/#research">Download this pinned research snapshot →</a></p><p>Declared companion fields help correlate these fixtures. They do not create a cross-database foreign key or an automatic join.</p></li>
 </> : <>
  <li><h2>Open {table.name} and select a record</h2><p><a class="text-link" href={`/tables/${encodeURIComponent(table.name)}/#data`}>Browse native rows →</a></p><p>Use row search and the record detail. The URL keeps supported filters and the selected primary key so you can return to the same context.</p><TableActions db={db} table={table} /></li>
  <li><h2>Follow relationships and explain the fields</h2><p>{db.id === 'chinook' ? 'Follow Track.AlbumId to Album, then Album.ArtistId to Artist. These are declared foreign keys. The MeaningGraph bindings explain business concepts separately.' : 'Open Relationships for declared foreign keys and a copyable join. Meanings explains the provider’s table and field bindings.'}</p><p><a class="text-link" href={`/tables/${encodeURIComponent(table.name)}/#relationships`}>Inspect relationships →</a> · <a class="text-link" href={`/tables/${encodeURIComponent(table.name)}/#meanings`}>Explain the meanings →</a></p></li>
  <li><h2>Run, inspect and change a query</h2><p>Open a prepared SQLite example below, inspect its input and expected result, then choose Run. Change the question and run again. Teaching-subset totals differ from the full database.</p><QueryExamples db={db} compact /></li>
  <li><h2>Continue with the full dataset</h2><p><a class="text-link" href="/downloads/">Choose a complete engine edition →</a> · <a class="text-link" href="/model/">Read the model and meaning contract →</a></p><p>Preserve the fixture revision, checksum and data licence when sharing your result.</p></li>
 </>}
 </ol></section>
</SiteLayout>
<style>.guided-journey>ol{padding-left:28px;max-width:1000px}.guided-journey>ol>li{padding:0 0 28px 12px;margin-bottom:24px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.guided-journey h2{font-size:26px}.guided-journey p{max-width:85ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8}.guided-journey code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}</style>
